invariant: INV-26
file: quic_step.c
catches: test/lint-quic-surface.sh
reason: quic_step.c spells the body of struct aes_public_key itself, so it
  declares a key and writes a traffic secret into one without including
  quic_aes_key.h at all. C diagnoses no mismatched struct definition
  across translation units, so this edit compiles clean in every
  compiler this tree uses and the incomplete type in quic_aes.h stops
  nothing: the file passes its own key to aes_encrypt_block and the
  S-box is indexed by the secret. The include allowlist alone read past
  this shape, because there is no include to read.
  tools/quic-footprint.py's key_holders() refuses a body outside
  quic_aes_key.h, and `make lint-quic-surface` is where it runs.

--- old
#include "quic_step.h"
--- new
#include "quic_step.h"
struct aes_public_key { uint8_t key[176]; uint8_t iv[12]; uint8_t hp[176]; };
